1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,220
In 1980 the US Department of Defense
wanted to know

2
00:00:04,260 --> 00:00:06,460
how the Red Army
could be stopped.

3
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:11,590
It asked a man whom a German court
had convicted in 1948:

4
00:00:11,630 --> 00:00:12,710
Hermann Balck.

5
00:00:12,750 --> 00:00:18,130
Born in Danzig in 1893, wounded
seven times in the First World War.

6
00:00:18,170 --> 00:00:23,910
On May 13, 1940, he led his rifle
regiment across the Meuse at Sedan.

7
00:00:23,950 --> 00:00:26,110
It was the breakthrough into France.

8
00:00:26,150 --> 00:00:30,310
In December 1942 he stood
with the 11th Panzer Division

9
00:00:30,350 --> 00:00:33,110
on the Chir River,
west of Stalingrad.

10
00:00:33,150 --> 00:00:35,460
A Soviet tank army attacked.

11
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:39,400
For a week Balck had his men
march by night and fight by day.

12
00:00:39,440 --> 00:00:44,480
With only about 25 tanks still fit for action,
he struck the attackers from behind.

13
00:00:44,520 --> 00:00:48,030
He rose to command
an army group.

14
00:00:48,070 --> 00:00:53,240
In autumn 1944 he fought in Lorraine
against George Patton's army.

15
00:00:53,280 --> 00:00:58,110
In November he had an artillery
commander shot there without trial

16
00:00:58,150 --> 00:01:00,420
because he had found him drunk.

17
00:01:00,460 --> 00:01:03,700
In December he was relieved
of command and sent to Hungary.

18
00:01:03,740 --> 00:01:06,960
At the end of the war
he became an American prisoner.

19
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:10,530
In 1948 a court in Stuttgart
sentenced him

20
00:01:10,570 --> 00:01:13,020
for this shooting
to three years in prison.

21
00:01:13,060 --> 00:01:14,970
He served 18 months.

22
00:01:15,010 --> 00:01:19,310
After that he lived in seclusion
and refused interviews for decades.

23
00:01:19,350 --> 00:01:22,600
Only in 1980 did he sit with
Friedrich von Mellenthin

24
00:01:22,640 --> 00:01:27,000
before American planners and explain
how to fight the Soviets.

25
00:01:27,040 --> 00:01:31,320
The US Army historian who
described the Lorraine campaign

26
00:01:31,360 --> 00:01:34,970
had called him
a convinced National Socialist.

27
00:01:35,010 --> 00:01:37,950
Hermann Balck died in 1982.

28
00:01:37,990 --> 00:01:40,230
They had asked him as a teacher.

29
00:01:40,270 --> 00:01:42,750
He had been convicted as a perpetrator.

30
00:01:42,790 --> 00:01:44,280
Did you know this story?

31
00:01:44,320 --> 00:01:46,060
Tell us in the comments!
